From fa49af507986732b46e576705fe7a61048035a7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 03:10:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] meta: feed images must be absolute, or Meta rejects the whole
 item

The first upload that ever reached Meta rejected all seven vehicles:

  Result: Item not uploaded
  Issue:  URL Incorrectly Formatted
  Field:  image

Every generated demo photo is generatedPhotoUrl() -> "/api/photo?s=...",
root-relative. That is correct in an <img> on our own page and unusable to
Meta, which fetches from its own infrastructure and has no origin to resolve
against. Nothing else in the row was wrong -- the landing-page url column built
from siteBase was absolute and accepted. One bad image URL rejects the item.

This was invisible everywhere it could have been caught locally. The
storefront, the admin gallery and the feed preview all render these photos
correctly, because they are all same-origin. The TSV looked well-formed. Only
Meta cared, and only after a fetch that had never happened until today.

photoBase is a new BuildOptions field, and it is the app origin rather than
siteBase: the two diverge the moment a dealer is on their own domain, where the
storefront is cascademotorswa.com but /api/photo is only ever served by the
app.

Absolute URLs pass through untouched -- a dealer's real CDN photos must not be
rewritten. An unresolvable relative photo is dropped rather than emitted
broken, and the remaining photos renumber so image[0] always exists: an item
with one fewer photo uploads, an item Meta refuses does not.

Three tests added, in the file reserved for feed bugs that produce a
valid-looking feed which quietly does not work. This is the fifth such mode.

tsc clean; 33/33 feed-spec tests pass; npm run build clean.

